# The FOUR positions a fixed array may NOT flow through, one file, one row each
# (panel 081 R3). Every one of these was `heroes check` exit 0 before the repair:
# the first two reached clang and came back as `internal error: compiling the
# generated C failed` (exit 2, the compiler blaming itself for the author's
# program, CLAUDE.md §7), and the third reached the runtime as
# `hero_unreachable` at exit 134.
#
# **It said THREE until 2026-09-19**, and the fourth is defect 064: an operand of
# an operator, found at panel 165 while pricing a route that would have opened
# this very position. It failed exactly as rows 1 and 2 did — exit 0 from the
# checker, then clang naming a temporary the emitter never defined — which is the
# guard's own paragraph in `selfhost/emit/gate.hero` arriving a fifth time. The
# count is stated here because nothing else counts these rows.
#
# WHY `.call` IS NOT A FIFTH ROW, though panel 165's completeness critic named it
# the unguarded sibling of `.binary`: a fixed array reaching a call is how
# `f.ptr()` and `f.validated_bytes()` work, so a blanket row on `.call` would
# refuse the two lends this language ships. What holds the rest of that position
# shut is `ffi_type` and `fixed_outside_a_group`, which is written here rather
# than left in the gate — the gate is at its `DECIDED` ceiling and this file has
# none, and the reason belongs with the rows either way.
#
# Cause, one for all three: a `T[N]` has no storage of its own in C —
# `float t[4]; t = …;` compiles at no optimisation level — so `emit/storageless.rs`
# renders one where it is USED rather than assigning it, and that works in exactly
# two positions: the base of a subscript, and an argument at the construction.
# Nothing refused the others.
#
# The header is local rather than a package, so this case is never skipped for a
# missing library. A skip is a pass, and these rows were crashes.
#
# What still works is in `tests/golden/run/ffi-a-c-array-member.hero`: reading by
# index, passing the whole record by value, `==`, and a map value. The refusal
# must not reach any of them.

extern "fixed-array-flow.h"
    record Lens
        x: f32
        y: f32
        reserved: i32[4]
    function lens_first(l: Lens) -> i32

function main()
    a = Lens(x: 1.0, y: 2.0, reserved: [7, 0, 0, 0])

    # 1. Given a name. `use of undeclared identifier 'h1_named'` before the row:
    #    the instruction that would define the local emits nothing, and the store
    #    that follows it still names it.
    named = a.reserved  #~ fixed_flow

    # 2. Copied into another record. This one DID render — as `t.reserved` — and
    #    that spelling is right as a subscript base and wrong as a C initialiser.
    b = Lens(x: 0.0, y: 0.0, reserved: a.reserved)  #~ fixed_flow

    # 3. As the element of a container: no descriptor, because it has no storage.
    lenses = [a.reserved]  #~ fixed_element

    # 4. As an operand of an operator — defect 064, found at panel 165 and added
    #    2026-09-19. `heroes check` exit 0, then clang: `use of undeclared
    #    identifier 't6'`, the compiler blaming itself a FIFTH time for the same
    #    cause. The record's own `==` still works and walks elementwise; what has
    #    no C value to stand on either side is the field alone.
    same = a.reserved == b.reserved  #~ fixed_flow
    print(named[0], b.x, len(lenses), same)
